A||||9||MinnGreenGT||Will and '87 Headlight assembly fit on an '86?||||5||
Z||000000||MinnGreenGT||10-31-2001||10:18 AM||||I understand that the '84-'86 Headlight assemblies are the same, but that '87-'88 are different than the rest.  Can a complete headllight assembly (unbolted from the car) be easily installed and wired into an '86?  Are the relays, plugs, and wiring the same?<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Smoooooth GT||10-31-2001||10:33 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MinnGreenGT:<BR><B>I understand that the '84-'86 Headlight assemblies are the same, but that '87-'88 are different than the rest.  Can a complete headllight assembly (unbolted from the car) be easily installed and wired into an '86?  Are the relays, plugs, and wiring the same?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Only if you replace your's with a set of Tom's..lol  Listen I have a 87GT part's car so I'm sure I can change all wiring -relay's, etc. to make them work. lmk, Steve<BR><P>------------------<BR>UNDER CONSTRUCTION      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooth_sig2_4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||MinnGreenGT||10-31-2001||10:48 AM||||  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  You've got mail.<P>BTW: I'm still curious for anyone who can answer this.<p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 10-31-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||pherder||10-31-2001||10:58 AM||||MinnGreenGT,<P>Yes and no.  The headlight motors will bolt into the headlight mechanism but the wiring will not work.<P>You need the "firewall" forward harness complete to make the 87-88 headlight motors work in an earlier Fiero.  Everything will bolt on/plug in.  The only problem will be running the wiring harness from the left side to the right side next to the radiator, under the front hood.  You also need the relay box that goes under the front driver's side fender (it controls the stopping of the motors, both up and down.)<P>I did this to my 86 SE.<P>Paul<p>[This message has been edited by pherder (edited 10-31-2001).]||||reg||1
